# Documentation: Bilingual Structure

When writing or editing files under `docs/`, use **two separate parts**. Do not mix English and Chinese in the same section or paragraph.

## Structure

1. **Part 1 — English only**  
   Write the full content in English first (titles, body, code comments in prose). No Chinese in this part.

2. **Part 2 — 中文 only**  
   After the English part, provide the same content entirely in Chinese. No English in this part.

## Format

- Use a clear separator between the two parts (e.g. `---`, or a heading like "中文说明").
- Keep section order and structure the same in both parts so readers can match them.
- Do not use inline mixing (e.g. avoid "架构总览 | High-Level Architecture" in one heading; use one language per part).

## Example

```markdown
# Module Overview

This module handles...

---

# 模块概览

本模块负责...
```
